mode: "100644"
text: "# Pipeline, formats, tools + two worked examples\n\n## Production pipeline\n```\n1 record -> 2 transcribe (Descript/Castmagic) -> 3 timestamp standout moments (+ retention spikes) ->\n4 generate 5-8 clips/audiograms (Opus Clip/Choppity/Headliner) -> 5 add hook + captions + branding ->\n6 strategic CTA -> 7 WoopSocial publishes across platforms on a cadence. (Full episode stays on the host.)\n```\n\n## Format decision + specs\n| You recorded | Format | Spec |\n|---|---|---|\n| Video | video-podcast clip | 9:16 (1080x1920), reframe to active speaker, captions, 30-90s |\n| Audio only | audiogram | cover art + animated waveform + captions + title; 9:16 / 1:1 / 16:9 |\n| One great line | quote card | on-brand graphic (-> design-and-templates) |\n\n## Tool table (verify-quarterly)\n| Job | Tool |\n|---|---|\n| Edit the episode | Descript (text-based, filler removal, publishes to Spotify/Apple/YT) |\n| Auto-clip video | Opus Clip (virality score, reframe) / Choppity (best conversational accuracy) / Kapwing (free) |\n| Audiograms | Headliner (waveform builder, Eddy AI, RSS) / Podsqueeze / Opus.pro |\n| Written repurposing | Castmagic (show notes/blog/captions/quotes) |\n| Caption burn-in (video clips) | -> captions-and-clipping / clipping.md |\n| Distribution scheduling | **WoopSocial** (publishes the finished files) |\nHonest: **Opus Clip is not an editor** -- little creative control; add the hook/overlay/CTA in another editor or via captions-and-clipping.\n\n## Audiogram anatomy\n```\n[ cover art / brand background ]  [ animated waveform: bars/circles/lines ]  [ burned-in captions ]  [ episode title + handle ]\nSave a template so every episode's audiograms match (-> design-and-templates). Export 9:16 / 1:1 / 16:9.\n```\n\n## CTA library (a reason to listen -- not \"check out the full episode\")\n```\n\"Find out why [guest] changed their mind -- full episode linked.\"   \"We argued about [topic] for 20 minutes. Hear who won.\"\n\"The part that surprised me is in the full episode.\"                 \"What would you do here? Full story in the episode.\"\n```\n\n## WoopSocial flow\n```\nagent plans the clips (retention-based) + writes hooks/CTAs + the cadence -> tool clips/generates -> creator finalizes\n-> WoopSocial publishes the finished clips/audiograms on schedule. WoopSocial does NOT record/edit/transcribe/clip/\ngenerate audiograms/host the podcast/pull retention. Captions non-optional. Never fabricate virality.\n```\n\n## Worked example 1 - video podcast (blunt indie-founder voice)\n```\n60-min video episode. I check YouTube Studio for the two replay spikes, pull those + 4 transcript moments = 6 clips. Opus Clip\nreframes to the speaker; I fix the hooks + add a real CTA (\"hear who won the argument -- full ep linked\"). Captions on all of\nthem, no exceptions. WoopSocial schedules them Tue/Thu/Sat across Reels/Shorts/TikTok + a LinkedIn quote card. The full ep stays on my host.\n```\n\n## Worked example 2 - audio-only show (warm studio voice)\n```\nAn audio-only interview show. We pick three warm, quotable moments from the transcript and build audiograms in Headliner -- our\ncover art, a gentle waveform, captions, the episode title -- all from a saved template so they match. Each ends with a reason to\nlisten, linked to the episode. We hand the finished audiograms to WoopSocial to publish across the week. Recording + hosting stay where they already live.\n```\n\nBoth: retention/transcript-led selection; the right format (clip vs audiogram); hook + captions (always) + a reason-to-listen\nCTA; on-brand template; WoopSocial publishes the finished files on a cadence; the full episode stays on the podcast host.\n"
